    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20782" root="سمل" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَوْمَلَةٌ</span></b>  <i>A small</i> [<i>cup of the kind called</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِنْجَانَة</span>,
(S, M, K, TA,) which latter is a post-classical
word, originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِلْجَانَة</span>: or the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سوملة</span>, as some
say, is <i>a small</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِيَالَجَة</span>, an arabicized word from
the Pers. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">پِيَالَهْ</span>; which is also called <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَرْجَهَارَةٌ</span>;
(TA;) and this is the same as the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِلْجَان</span>. (TA
voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طرجهارة</span>.)

